[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#E67E22]The Engineering: A Deeper Dive[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[B]1. Algorithmic Spatial Memory - No More "Brute-Force Guessing"[/B]
Without spatial indexing, teleportation is a guessing game. Profiling vanilla generation reveals the challenge: the Overworld is ~45% ocean, and the End is ~33% void. Standard RTPs waste immense resources loading and discarding these chunks.
[B]Our Solution:[/B] RTP uses advanced mapping to plot out your world's geometry. When it encounters a massive ocean or unsafe biome, it remembers that area. As the server runs, RTP dynamically shrinks its searchable area, skipping known "bad sectors" entirely without ever needing to load those chunks again. [B]The longer it runs, the faster it gets.[/B]

[B]2. Zero-Latency Execution Engine - Taming the Tick[/B]
Traditional RTPs cause unpredictable MSPT spikes by flooding the server with random, un-paced chunk requests. [B]RTP subverts this by enforcing strict structural caps.[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Pre-Warmed Background Caching:[/B] Our background pipeline continuously paces chunk evaluations, ensuring safe locations are ready before a player ever requests one.
[*][B]Native Folia Support:[/B] Built to respect Folia's regionized multi-threading using non-blocking execution to eliminate unnecessary scheduling delays.
[*][B]Zero-Leak Resource Management:[/B] We utilize transient in-memory tickets and an active watchdog to aggressively recover abandoned chunks and prevent the RAM bloat and world corruption caused by older force-loading methods.
[/LIST]

